<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.1.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00059</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.1.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>ad814c24-fa11-43ac-8b7b-624492f11751</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>For questions 1 – 5, use the following scenario to identify the expression, equation, or inequality described.</para>
<blockquote>
  <para>To support a local senior citizens center, a student club sent a flier home to the \(n\) students in the school. The flier said, “Please bring in money to support the senior citizens center. Paper money and coins accepted!” Their goal is to raise \(T\) dollars.</para>
</blockquote>
<para>Choose the expression, equation, or inequality, from the list, that describes the given quantity. </para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="c5eb8b61-7fbc-4523-a1ec-a4cc7ec0eba3"><problem><para>
      <para> The dollar amount the club would have if they
          reached half of their goal. </para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(T+50\)</para><para>\(0.5T\)</para><para>\(0.25n\)</para><para>\(0.5n\)</para><para>\(T-0.5n\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(0.5T\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(0.5T\). </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="2d9c7397-563f-467a-b604-3775cea9aa44"><problem><para>
      <para>For questions 7 - 8, determine if each is an expression or an equation that represents the English phrase</para>
      <para> 3(\(x\) − 7) = 27 </para>
      </para></problem><solution><para>equation</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is equation. </para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section><section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="143f01d5-22fa-4aa0-bb7a-c47383bb89b6"><problem><para>
      <para>For questions 9 - 10, choose the algebraic expression that represents the English phrase</para>
      <para>the
          difference of \(14x\) ² and 13 </para>
      </para><para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(14x^2 + 13\)</para><para>\(14x^2 - 13\)</para><para>\(13 - 14x^2\)</para><para>\(\frac{14x^2}{13}\)</para></problem><solution><para>\(14x^2 - 13\)</para><para>
      <para>The correct answer is \(14x^2-13\). You seem to be stuck who can you ask for help?</para>
    </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
